        </param>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Set the maximum amount of simulation time we&apos;ll allow to pass per frame. Normally, if the main loop is slow we&apos;ll run multiple simulation steps per frame to keep the game running at constant time. However if the main loop falls below this value, we&apos;ll cap how many simulation steps we run and start running the game loop slower. This can happen on slow machines, frame spikes, large file IO, or debugger breakpoints. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
